I wrote the Day 270 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (about 10 KB). The commit didn't happen: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. The instructions allow that (|| true), and the planner reads the file from disk.

Build and recent work
• The binary works: -p "Reply with exactly: ok" returned ok with exit 0, and config get model resolves claude-opus-5-5.
• The last 4 finished evolve runs succeeded. The 10 sessions in the trajectory window each completed 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts. The work has been concentrated on the bash safety checks.

Two files the next task could break by size
• src/context.rs is 2035 lines and has no entry in the size register. 15 more lines makes cargo test fail, which reverts the whole task.
• src/format/mod.rs is 86 lines past its recorded size. 14 more lines makes cargo test fail.

New findings
1. GPT-6.2 Sol tool calls go to the wrong endpoint. I pointed yoyo at a local recording server with --provider openai --model gpt-6.2-sol. It sent 12 tools to /chat/completions and warned that the model is unknown. OpenAI's GPT-6.2 guide says tool calling requires the Responses API, so tool calls likely fail on this model; I didn't test against OpenAI itself (no key). GPT-6.2 Sol has been Codex's default model since Nov 20. The cause is that openai_preset matches only five exact model ids. yoagent 0.27.9 already sorts this id to the Responses API (ModelConfig::generic). This is row 1 of #1060.
2. `yoyo doctor` reports healthy with a bogus key. With ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=bogus it prints "12/12 checks passed", because it never contacts the provider. Claude Code added a connectivity check to its own doctor on Nov 23. src/commands_dev.rs is at 1975 lines, so the check would need its own module.
3. Claude Code's changelog backs #1229. Their Nov 20 release makes rm aimed at the working folder ask first, and refuses it when nobody can answer. That is the case #1229 says yoyo still misses.

Suggested order for the planner: the GPT-6.2 fix, then #1229, then the next slice of #1184 (the read_array callers in config_value.rs), then the doctor check. #1233, #1215, #1239 and #1202 should stay untouched: they wait on @yuanhao, whose last activity in this repo was 2026-11-15T15:28Z (checked through the comments API).

